WEBVTT

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.833
Renewal season is paperwork season.

00:00:06.883 --> 00:00:13.419
The records your certifier asks for already exist, in your head, in a notebook, in a truck.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:19.100
So log them once, as you work. Pick what you did. Say it, or type it.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.566
Trazo prints back what it heard and fills the fields it can.

00:00:23.616 --> 00:00:27.587
You review every one of them before anything is saved.

00:00:28.563 --> 00:00:35.632
Name the product, and Trazo looks it up in the OMRI, WSDA and National List catalogues on file.

00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:40.352
The listing is OMRI's, Trazo just resolves the name against it.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:49.529
And before it saves, it tells you which of those details are for your certifier only, and will never appear on the page your buyer sees.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:57.332
If a detail your certifier will ask for is still blank, Trazo says so now, while you still remember.

00:00:57.382 --> 00:00:59.394
The record saves either way.

00:00:59.916 --> 00:01:05.317
Your crew logs in Spanish. You read the records in English. Same entry.

00:01:09.741 --> 00:01:14.862
Back at the desk, the season is on the calendar, every entry your crew made.

00:01:14.912 --> 00:01:19.898
Open one, and the whole record is there. Once the season closes, it locks.

00:01:19.948 --> 00:01:21.803
A correction leaves a trail.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:28.037
Your farm home runs the record checks a certifier runs, cited to the section.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:32.980
The readiness checks are ours. The findings are your certifier's.

00:01:33.806 --> 00:01:41.315
One entry. Two outputs. The record your certifier reviews. And the page your buyer scans.

00:01:41.815 --> 00:01:47.299
Those activities are your Organic System Plan. The modules fill from what you entered.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:57.865
And Trazo lists what changed on your operation since you last wrote your plan, ground you brought in, a production you closed, a certificate that arrived.

00:01:57.915 --> 00:02:02.472
Your annual update starts from your own year, not from last year's copy.

00:02:03.318 --> 00:02:14.125
When renewal opens, the packet is one download, plan narrative, annual update, change notifications, the module PDFs, the attachment workbooks.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.706
Filed with a date. What you sent, and when.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:32.400
And when the inspector asks for records, the audit dossier: input application log, purchase traceability, mass balance, sales, under 7 CFR 205.103.

00:02:33.197 --> 00:02:40.725
In California, the monthly pesticide use report compiles from the same spray records, ready to file in minutes.

00:02:41.463 --> 00:02:47.184
And with your permission, your certifier can open your records before the inspection.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:50.918
The readiness checks are ours; the findings are theirs.

00:02:51.759 --> 00:02:57.265
When the season is done, finish it. The harvest weight, a lot number, a grade.

00:02:57.315 --> 00:03:02.893
Publish the buyer page, and the same records become a page your buyer can scan.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:06.657
Practices, dates, photos, in plain language.

00:03:06.707 --> 00:03:12.068
And where the material is in a public catalogue, the page names which one.

00:03:12.118 --> 00:03:14.481
Where it isn't, it says that too.

00:03:15.324 --> 00:03:16.499
Not everything.

00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:25.078
Your applicator's name, registration numbers, rates and concentrations, removed before the page is built.

00:03:25.128 --> 00:03:32.186
A certifier is entitled to those. A shopper isn't. Same policy for every farm on Trazo.

00:03:32.236 --> 00:03:33.330
Not a setting.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:39.522
And if you ever want out, every record exports as a spreadsheet, on the free tier.

00:03:39.572 --> 00:03:43.151
On Compliance, the whole binder prints as a PDF too.

00:03:43.201 --> 00:03:46.850
Worst case, you are back to paper, with better paper.

00:03:47.589 --> 00:03:51.126
Trazo doesn't certify your farm. Your certifier does.

00:03:51.176 --> 00:03:54.510
Trazo gets you to the table with complete records.

00:03:55.063 --> 00:03:59.539
Start free. No card, no clock. trazo.io
